[gd_scene load_steps=7 format=3 uid="uid://unittextmesh"]

; The one variable: the surface a TextMesh builds from the outlines of a TrueType scene font. The left
; text has depth, so its sides catch the light and its front takes the top of the texture. The right
; text has none, so one face shows the whole texture. The gradient runs red, green, blue along the
; U + V diagonal and the material is unshaded, so each band shows where the UVs land. The glyphs 8, a
; and A hold the holes and the curves that the tessellation must keep.

